      "message": "I still think we should just WARN_ON here. iommu_suspend() doesn\u0027t seem to be the right place for printing logs like \"pKVM does not support S3 suspend\", since S3 is not about IOMMU, and iommu_suspend() is just one of many S3-specific suspend callbacks in the kernel. (Also, ratelimiting is not quite needed in this case?)\n\nAnd again, per the above, if we reached iommu_suspend() while pKVM is enabled, we are already in a pretty bad unrecoverable state, so a noisy WARN_ON seems more appropriate?",
